\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Discussion}
\title{Unequal arcs after one removal}
\date{2026-11-06}

\p{Decimation by #{2}, as in \ref{fdip-00AX}, removes every other
vertex of a [uniform cycle precision](fdip-00AW). The arcs that remain are
equal. The calculation that follows asks what precision is left
when one vertex is removed from between two arcs that need not
be equal. The data are the cyclic order and the lengths of the
arcs. No covariance on a continuum is supplied.}
